WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
A diagnostic report should make the evidence mean something.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.280
Start with a referral and relevant history, then bring

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.660
together testing, samples, observations, and caregiver reports. When different

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.860
sources support the same pattern, you have converging evidence.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.020
When they disagree, pause and investigate the difference. Test,

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.480
suitability, fatigue, participation, and task demands can affect what

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.540
you observe. Neither the standardized score nor the everyday

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.660
report automatically cancels the other.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:31.390
Now move from data to meaning. A result states

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:35.550
what happened, such as omitted grammatical markers. Interpretation explains

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.990
the skill suggested by that pattern. The clinical impression

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:43.150
integrates the communication profile across sources, including strengths, functional

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:47.570
impact, and limitations. Diagnosis identifies the disorder supported by

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:50.210
the complete evidence. Repeating a score is not the

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:53.070
same as explaining it. A severity label also needs

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:55.990
assessment support, not a judgment that the performance looked

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:56.270
bad.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.660
Differential diagnosis keeps competing explanations open until the findings

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:06.700
distinguish them. For reduced intelligibility, investigate specific sound production,

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.620
phonological patterns, motor planning, and hearing. Repeated productions, transitions,

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.260
and prosody help investigate a motor planning concern. Hearing

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.940
information addresses auditory access change the hypothesis when the

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.000
evidence changes. If comprehension is a relative strength and

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.500
expression remains weak, investigate an expressive disorder rather than

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:26.960
forcing a mixed language label.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.460
Recommendations should follow findings you can point to in

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.380
the report. Use strengths such as social engagement to

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:36.440
support planning, but do not assume social interest proves

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.360
intact pragmatic language. Explain how the difficulty affects daily

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.400
communication. Link language needs to appropriate targets, hearing concerns

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:48.580
to audiological follow -up, and unresolved inconsistency to further

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.740
assessment. A recommendation without supporting findings needs repair. Clear

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.340
documentation supports reasoning. It does not guarantee coverage.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.050
Finally, separate the condition from the service. ICD -10

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:05.450
-CM identifies the diagnosis. CPT identifies what the clinician

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:09.370
performed. The course pairs F80 .2 with Mixed Receptive

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:13.630
Expressive Language Disorder. It pairs 92523 with a combined

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:16.970
speech sound production and language evaluation. Treatment is a

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:20.510
different service from evaluation. A recommendation for future therapy

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:23.370
does not mean therapy was provided today. Let the

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:26.030
evidence support the diagnosis and let the completed service

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:27.170
determine its service code.
